title: Remove try_state(false) escape hatch from pallet-staking-async tests

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The `LastValidatorEra` consistency check in `check_paged_exposures`
      (try-state) is promoted from a log-only warning to a hard error. For each
      validator in the active era's exposures, the entry must be the active
      era, the active era + 1 once the validator's exposure for the next era
      is stored, or absent (stash reaped or force-unstaked mid-era; a warning
      is logged if it is still bonded). This changes try-runtime strictness
      only. No production runtime behavior is affected.

      The pallet's test mock no longer lets a test skip the post-test
      `do_try_state` check: `ExtBuilder::try_state(false)` and the
      `SkipTryStateCheck` flag are removed, and tests that corrupt storage on
      purpose restore it before the closure exits.

crates:
  - name: pallet-staking-async
    bump: patch
